Fleet Manager is a personal software project published publicly
for portfolio, demonstration, and professional evaluation purposes.
Its primary purpose is to showcase software development skills,
architectural decisions, coding practices, and the implementation
of a full-stack application.

The source code is made available for inspection and review so that
recruiters, employers, and other interested individuals can evaluate
the technical aspects of the project and the skills demonstrated
through its development.

Public access to this repository does not mean that the project
is open-source software or that permission is granted to reuse
its source code.

